# ABI v1 obligation 12.5: the concurrency suite
#   width table: per context, prefix moved on a miss -- ABI v1 section 6 as SHIPPED
#   guard:       on
#   shapes:      P1.2 and P2.2 (M1 leaf, M2 non-leaf), plus P1.3 and P2.5
#   vCPUs:       4

## 1. the reference: prost, the INCUMBENT's encoder

shape         bytes
P1.2         218121
P2.2         540422
P1.3            605
P2.5          19632

# NOT a re-encode with the code under test. Section 6: only the COMBINATION of
# its two refusals corrupts, and it corrupts so that the threads agree with each
# other -- so a suite comparing two threads, or comparing against a reference
# taken with the same polluted encoder, finds nothing. It takes an independent
# encoder, and prost is one: different codec, different object graph, itself
# checked against the validated manifest by gen/stage2.sh.

## 1b. what each oracle sees

encodes from a context with history                   8
wrong against PROST (the oracle now)                  0
wrong against a fresh core-ffi context (the old oracle)          0

# Nothing to find on this build, and both oracles agree that there is
# nothing -- which is what the change to the oracle has to cost: zero.

## 2. SEQUENCE: two shapes alternating on ONE context, one thread

  encodes 40, wrong 0
  decodes 40, wrong 0

# The one-shape control, which is the comparison obligation 12.5 asks for:
  one shape (P1.2) on one context, 40 encodes, wrong 0
# A per-shape-state defect is invisible to that row by construction and
# visible to the rotation above. That is why the obligation says two shapes.

## 3. TOGETHER: N threads, one context each, all four shapes (P1.2, P2.2, P1.3, P2.5) rotated per round

threads         encodes      wrong decodes wrong
2                   400          0            0
4                   800          0            0
8                  1600          0            0

# 8 threads on 4 vCPUs is deliberate: oversubscription puts a preemption
# between a `begin` and its `end`, which is where a state defect that needs a
# window to open would show. R9 is the caveat on the other side -- a
# concurrency figure from a small container is a lower bound on contention,
# and section 5 below is the figure, not this section.

